# scripts/cia-tools.env — pinned CIA-packaging tool releases (docs/DESIGN.md
# §8.3, risk 11). Sourced by clients/3ds/build.sh's `cia` action and by
# .github/workflows/ci.yml's client-3ds job's tag-gated .cia steps. Not
# read by scripts/build.sh's core/server/tools/3ds targets, and not read
# by the ordinary (untagged) client-3ds CI steps — only the .cia path.
#
# Different shape from scripts/toolchains.env on purpose: those are
# container image digests (`docker manifest inspect`); these are GitHub
# release archive URLs with a pinned sha256, because neither tool below is
# distributed as a container image. Same rule applies regardless of shape:
# pin by tag/digest, verify the asset actually exists before pinning, never
# reference `latest`/a moving branch. Regenerate by hand (no
# pin-toolchains.sh-equivalent script exists for these yet — GitHub release
# assets, not `docker pull`able images) and re-verify with sha256sum before
# committing a new pin.

# makerom (3DSGuy/Project_CTR) — compiles in seconds from source per
# docs/DESIGN.md §8.2/§8.3, but v0.19.0 (2026-01-18) also ships a prebuilt Linux
# x86_64 binary, which is simpler and faster than a from-source build step
# in every CI run. Verified 2026-08-10: downloaded, sha256-checked against
# the digest below, and run (`makerom -help`) successfully inside the
# pinned devkitARM container (scripts/toolchains.env DEVKITARM) and
# natively — same x86_64 binary works in both.
MAKEROM_VERSION=makerom-v0.19.0
MAKEROM_LINUX_URL=https://github.com/3DSGuy/Project_CTR/releases/download/makerom-v0.19.0/makerom-v0.19.0-ubuntu_x86_64.zip
MAKEROM_LINUX_SHA256=287b809dec064e0ad597e3d272c49ecb7eed41693d5ee6fef9d8a8aa24c2497e

# bannertool is deliberately NOT fetched by CI or scripts/build.sh —
# docs/DESIGN.md §8.3 / risk 11's documented fallback. Confirmed 2026-08-10 that
# the risk is real, not hypothetical: github.com/Steveice10/bannertool
# returns 404 — the repository is gone, not merely archived/stale.
# clients/3ds/meta/banner.bnr and clients/3ds/meta/icon.icn are prebuilt
# outputs, committed directly, and fed straight to makerom
# (clients/3ds/Makefile's `cia` target) — no bannertool invocation exists
# in the build path CI or scripts/build.sh runs.
#
# The two lines below record what produced the CURRENTLY COMMITTED
# clients/3ds/meta/banner.bnr and icon.icn, for reproducibility only, so a
# future replacement of the placeholder art (clients/3ds/meta/banner.png,
# icon.png, audio.wav) can be rebuilt the same way by hand:
#   bannertool makebanner -i clients/3ds/meta/banner.png \
#     -a clients/3ds/meta/audio.wav -o clients/3ds/meta/banner.bnr
#   bannertool makesmdh -s "AtticPad" -l "AtticPad Controller" \
#     -p "AtticPad" -i clients/3ds/meta/icon.png -o clients/3ds/meta/icon.icn
# Source used: carstene1ns/3ds-bannertool (a maintained, NOT archived
# backup of Steveice10/bannertool with a CMake build system and prebuilt
# Linux releases — confirmed not archived and last released 2026-06-13,
# i.e. actively maintained, not itself a second archived dependency).
# Re-pin and re-verify sha256 before regenerating — do not trust these
# values blindly if months have passed.
BANNERTOOL_VERSION_USED_FOR_COMMITTED_ASSETS=1.2.3
BANNERTOOL_LINUX_URL_USED_FOR_COMMITTED_ASSETS=https://github.com/carstene1ns/3ds-bannertool/releases/download/1.2.3/bannertool-1.2.3-linux.tar.gz
BANNERTOOL_LINUX_SHA256_USED_FOR_COMMITTED_ASSETS=748519d200519db18e9fd00c332ac32f5411e41230258291e89953a76c1f7155
